.TH "INSPEKT\-LINKS" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-links \- Extract all links from the current page.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]links\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Extract all links from the current page.
.PP
Returns structured data including link text, URLs, and link types
(internal, external, anchor).
Uses the live DOM, so it sees JavaScript\-rendered content that simple
HTML parsing would miss.
.PP
Can filter by link type and include/exclude anchor links.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enonly\-internal\f[R]
Show only internal links (same domain)
.TP
\f[B]\(enonly\-external\f[R]
Show only external links (different domain)
.TP
\f[B]\(enalphabetically\f[R]
Sort links alphabetically
.TP
\f[B]\(enonly\-urls\f[R]
Show only URLs without anchor text
.TP
\f[B]\(enjson\f[R]
Output as JSON with detailed link information
.TP
\f[B]\(enenrich\-external\f[R]
Fetch additional metadata for external links (MIME type, file size, page
title, language, HTTP status)
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
inspekt links
inspekt links \-\-filter external
inspekt links \-\-no\-anchors
inspekt links \-\-only\-internal
inspekt links \-\-only\-external
inspekt links \-\-alphabetically
inspekt links \-\-only\-urls
inspekt links \-\-only\-external \-\-only\-urls
inspekt links \-\-enrich\-external
.EE
